      <memberdef kind="variable" id="constants_8hpp_1a53b1dd65b593ae0971a3d16073e44bad" prot="public" static="no" constexpr="yes" mutable="no">
        <type>constexpr double</type>
        <definition>constexpr double CAR_HASNT_MOVED_START_RADIUS</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>CAR_HASNT_MOVED_START_RADIUS</name>
        <initializer>= 0.3</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>When the car is in start position, we want the path to recalculate not from car&apos;s closest midpoint but from 0 (empty <ref refid="classTrace" kindref="compound">Trace</ref>). To do this we need to know if the car is in a starting position. We will recalculate path from scratch (see <ref refid="classTrace_1a938a138ddd37dff4e25f2608713827a0" kindref="member">Trace::trimByLocal()</ref>) basically if car&apos;s outside a radius from (0,0). </para>
        </briefdescription>
